If Zod validation fails, you can catch the error and return an object with error details. Use `safeParse` instead of `parse` to avoid throwing:

```js
const result = postSchema.safeParse(data);
if (!result.success) return { error: result.error.issues[0].message };
```

Then `useFormState` receives `{ error: '...' }` and you can display it.
